{
  "title": "92: al-Layl الليل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(1)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YAGHSHAA.\nBy the night when it envelops,\nوَالنَّهَارِ اِذَا تَجَلّٰىۙ‏(2)\nWAN NAHAARE EZAA TAJALLAA.\nby the day when it brightens,\nوَمَا خَلَقَ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰٓىۙ‏(3)\nWA MAA KHALAQAZ ZAKARA WAL UNSAA.\nby Him who created the male and the female:\nاِنَّ سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتّٰىؕ‏(4)\nINNA SA’YAKUM LA-SHATTAA.\nyour endeavours are indeed diverse.\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ اَعْطٰى وَاتَّقٰىۙ‏(5)\nFA-AMMAA MAN A-A’TAA WAT TAQAA.\nAs for him who gives and is Godwary\nوَصَدَّقَ بِالْحُسْنٰىۙ‏(6)\nWA SADDAQA BIL-HUSNAA.\nand confirms the best promise,\nفَسَنُيَسِّرُهٗ لِلْيُسْرٰىؕ‏(7)\nFASANOYASSEROHU LIL-YUSRAA.\nWe will surely ease him toward facility.\nوَاَمَّا مَنْۢ بَخِلَ وَاسْتَغْنٰىۙ‏(8)\nWA AMMAA MAM BAKHELA WAS TAGHNAA.\nBut as for him, who is stingy and self-complacent,\nوَكَذَّبَ بِالْحُسْنٰىۙ‏(9)\nWA KAZZABA BIL-HUSNAA.\nand denies the best promise,\nفَسَنُيَسِّرُهٗ لِلْعُسْرٰىؕ‏(10)\nFASANOYASSEROHU LIL-U’SRAA.\nWe will surely ease him toward hardship.\nوَمَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُ مَالُهٗۤ اِذَا تَرَدّٰىؕ‏(11)\nWA MAA YUGHNEE A’NHO MAALOHU EZAA TARADDAA.\nHis wealth will not avail him when he perishes.\nاِنَّ عَلَيْنَا لَلْهُدٰىۖ‏(12)\nINNA A’LAYNAA LAL-HODAA.\nIndeed guidance rests with Us,\nوَاِنَّ لَنَا لَلْاٰخِرَةَ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(13)\nWA INNA LANAA LAL-AAKHERATA WAL OOLAA.\nand to Us belong the world and the Hereafter.\nفَاَنْذَرْتُكُمْ نَارًا تَلَظّٰىۚ‏(14)\nFA-ANZARTOKUM NAARAN TALAZZAA.\nSo I warn you of a blazing fire,\nلَا يَصْلٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا الْاَشْقَىۙ‏(15)\nLAA YASLAAHAA ILLAL ASHQAL.\nwhich none shall enter except the most wretched [of persons]\nالَّذِىْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىؕ‏(16)\nLAZEE KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\n—he who impugns [God’s prophets] and turns his back.\nوَسَيُجَنَّبُهَا الْاَتْقَىۙ‏(17)\nWA SAYOJANNABOHAL ATQAL.\nThe Godwary [person] will be spared of that\nالَّذِىْ يُؤْتِىْ مَالَهٗ يَتَزَكّٰىۚ‏(18)\nLAZEE YOATEE MAALAHU UATAZAKKAA.\n—he who gives his wealth to purify himself\nوَمَا لِاَحَدٍ عِنْدَهٗ مِنْ نِّعْمَةٍ تُجْزٰٓىۙ‏(19)\nWA MAA LE-AHADIN I’NDAHU MIN NEA’MATIN TUJZAA.\nand does not expect any reward from anyone,\nاِلَّا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِ الْاَعْلٰىۚ‏(20)\nILLAAB TEGHAAA-A WAJHE RABBEHIL A-A’LAA.\nbut seek only the pleasure of their Lord, the Most Exalted,\nوَلَسَوْفَ يَرْضٰى‏(21)\nWA LASAWFA YARZAA.\nand, surely, soon they will be well-pleased.",
  "merits": "There are 21 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward of reciting this Surah is so much that the one who recites it will be pleased when he sees it in his Book of Deeds. His inspiration of good deeds (Tawfiq) will also increase.\nIf recited 15 times before sleeping, one will dream about what pleases him most. Reciting it in the Isha prayers carries the reward of completing a quarter of the Holy Qur’an and is guaranteed that the prayers are accepted."
